OMI Morelos — browser C++ compiler

The browser compiler vendors Clang 8.0.1, LLD, memfs, the C/C++ WASI
sysroot, and an adapted JavaScript runtime from:
  https://github.com/binji/wasm-clang
  Revision: 648c4a89997a351eef75cdaec3ef5b89d4937dec
  Original copyright: 2020 WebAssembly Community Group participants

The JavaScript runtime and memfs are covered by LICENSE (Apache-2.0).
LLVM/Clang, LLD, libc++, libc++abi and compiler-rt are covered by
LICENSE.llvm (Apache-2.0 with LLVM exceptions and the included legacy
LLVM license). Existing header copyright/license notices remain in
sysroot.tar.gz.bin. The sysroot also contains the WASI libc distribution;
its license is reproduced in LICENSE.wasi-libc.

Local changes (2026):
- runtime.js preserves the original copyright header and adds UTF-8 I/O,
  separate stdout/stderr, corrected wasm32 argument/environment size and
  pointer-array handling, memory refresh for random_get, clock_time_get,
  an empty environment and no imported canvas/browser capabilities.
- The memory section of the Clang and LLD WASM binaries now has a maximum
  of 4096 pages (256 MiB each); memfs has 1024 pages (64 MiB). These are
  limits on each linear memory, not the total browser process memory.
- Compiler assets are gzip-compressed deterministically. The .bin suffix
  prevents static hosts from applying automatic HTTP decompression.
  manifest.json records upstream and modified uncompressed SHA-256 hashes.
- worker.js adds a fresh virtual filesystem per run, a standard-header
  bits/stdc++.h compatibility header, fixed C++17 flags, compiler-rt
  linking, UTF-8 output limits, cache validation and phase messages.
  Compiled student programs have a 128 MiB linear-memory maximum.

The compiler/runtime distributions have their own licenses and are not
relicensed under the curriculum's Creative Commons license.
